  "name": "Example: \n                    Translating Between Phrases and Algebraic Expressions Containing Addition",
  "problem": "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The sum of three and a number.\"",
  "worked_solution": "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the sum of three and a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\n3+x.\n$$\n\n**Note:** There are other correct answers as well. We could choose another letter, such as $a$, to represent the number. In that case, \"the sum of three and a number\" could also be written as \n\n$$\n3+a.\n$$",
